  "cde4a532-a212-419e-9c71-030095a3c336": {
   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p5-teaching",
     "replacement": "Recall that a trial is one repetition of an experiment.\n\n**Frequency** is how often something happens.\n\n**Expected frequency** is the number of times we expect an event to happen in a given number of trials.\n\n$$\\begin{gathered}\\text{Expected}\\\\\\text{frequency}\\end{gathered}=\\begin{gathered}\\text{Number of}\\\\\\text{trials}\\end{gathered}\\times\\text{Probability}$$\n\n$$f=np$$\n\nTo find expected frequency, where $n$ is the number of trials and $p$ is the probability of the event:\n\n1. Find the probability.\n2. Multiply the number of trials by the probability.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p5-teaching",
     "targetFingerprint": "ed5e852cfa56da585cb4f4b7767de186484d7936dd221316d64a1c9cf015cc60",
