    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p6-complement-definition-block",
     "replacement": "The **complement** of an event $E$ is the event that $E$ does **not** happen. It is written $\\bar E$ and contains every outcome in $S$ that is not in $E$.\n\nAn event and its complement have no outcomes in common, and together they make up the sample space.\n\n$$E\\cup\\bar E=S$$",
