     "replacement": "For a multistage experiment in which the number of ways each stage can occur does not depend on the earlier stages:\n\nIf one stage can occur in $m$ ways and the next stage in $n$ ways,\nthen both stages can occur in $m\\times n$ ways. For more stages, multiply the numbers of ways at every stage.",
